    "within": "Questions 1 to 3 tap-count a scattered group of 3, then 4, then 5. Question 4 builds a set of 3 or 4. Question 5 types the count of a messy group of 4 or 5. Question 6 picks which group has 4. Questions 7 to 8 stretch the count sequence (next after 4, then order 1 to 4). Question 9 matches 2 to 5 with pictures. Question 10 asks how many in a messy 5. No return to a 1-object count.",
    "versus": "Easy: tidy rows, counts 1 to 5 in order, hints on items 1 to 3. Medium: scattered layouts, mixed pictures and numerals, build and type counts can move inside 3 to 5, hints only on 1 to 3. Hard: extra objects to ignore, number words, a full 1 to 5 order, and almost no hints. Still counting to 5, not bonds."
